                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "08e6adb1-efe6-3da6-9bac-8d8e9b537034",
                        "entry_id": "cccba3b1-8550-388f-a44c-51102a9a49a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To locate by means of triangulation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "df8c9113-a355-4dae-94ef-2f68972e3057",
                                "sense_id": "08e6adb1-efe6-3da6-9bac-8d8e9b537034",
                                "text": "\"I'll give you a check now,\" I said abruptly, and saw Selina's green eyes triangulate angrily on my face."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d24406fb-58ac-3b34-9516-759b6569d799",
                        "entry_id": "cccba3b1-8550-388f-a44c-51102a9a49a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To pit two others against each other in order to achieve a desired outcome or to gain an advantage; to \\\"play both sides against the middle\\\"."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7641fd2-0b02-4b69-a1de-9ac688ac3a31",
                                "sense_id": "d24406fb-58ac-3b34-9516-759b6569d799",
                                "text": "Cruz, meanwhile, could wind up in the hot seat as he tries to triangulate between his disagreement with Trump’s position and his clear unwillingness to openly attack."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d607ecf5-6c7c-4949-8126-dfc645bae0b5",
                                "sense_id": "d24406fb-58ac-3b34-9516-759b6569d799",
                                "text": "By attempting to triangulate, Labour convinced leavers it was for remain and remainers that it was for leave. The party looked cynical and opportunistic, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9abb1249-0211-463a-b490-96d4c0a1ae44",
                                "sense_id": "d24406fb-58ac-3b34-9516-759b6569d799",
                                "text": "Triangulating after a midterm loss is a tried-and-true tactic for improving an administration’s position, yet it’s a tactic that the Biden Democrats largely eschewed: There was no Clintonian push for a sweeping legislative deal on deficit reduction, no serious outreach on social issues, no reconsideration of the aggressive efforts to regulate gas-powered cars or forgive student loans, and only a too-little-too-late effort to restore order to the southern border."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ced767cf-e800-3e7e-9939-30759fa0e0c5",
                        "entry_id": "cccba3b1-8550-388f-a44c-51102a9a49a5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To divide into triangles."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cda98025-14a8-40e4-82df-068f20d0de3a",
                        "source_entry_id": "cccba3b1-8550-388f-a44c-51102a9a49a5",
